          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "meaning unknown in earliest occurrences (measured in dozens); turmeric, the aromatic and pungent root-stock of the East Indian plant (Curcuma longa), or the powder made of this, the chief ingredient in curry powder, used also in dyeing yellow, and as a chemical test, and in the East as a condiment and medicinally; also applied by English herbalists to the root of Tormentil, and to the root-stock of Sanguinaria canadensis (OED s.v. turmeric n. 1)"
    }
  ],
